L124@P2: Model Adjustment Impacts. When pruning methods are applied to LLMs they achieve
L125@P2: strong accuracy retention. On LLaMA-2-70B (Touvron et al., 2023), mean accuracy on
L126@P2: the EleutherAI LM Harness (Gao et al., 2021) decreases by only 7.13% with Magnitude
L127@P2: pruning and 2.94% with Wanda (Sun et al., 2023b), despite imposing a strict 2:4 structured
L128@P2: sparsity on the original model and removing 50% of weights. Beyond pruning, other forms
L129@P2: of weight adjustment have been widely studied, such as machine unlearning (Golatkar et al.,
L130@P2: 2020; Liu et al., 2024c) and fine-tuning (Hu et al., 2022). These studies demonstrate that
L131@P2: modifying weights can strongly affect downstream behavior: fine-tuning, for instance, has
L132@P2: been shown to degrade LLM safety (Yang et al., 2025; Huang et al.), motivating postfinetuning frameworks to preserve alignment (Djuhera et al., 2025; Hsu et al., 2024). Taken
